+RUVOjfrIemY,UCXzNNA2ngRpRiWvyA7eGd6w,Nick Invests,Why Your Credit Score Drops Even When You Pay On Time,5344,WEAK,2026-09-11,COMPLETE_LIMITED_EVIDENCE,FULL_TRANSCRIPT_TOPIC,"[""VIDEO_MASTER.csv:RUVOjfrIemY"", ""TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:RUVOjfrIemY"", ""audit-batches/NICK_153_READ_RECEIPTS.json""]","Credit-score mechanics explainer: why a score falls without missed payments (utilization snapshot timing, limit cuts, hard inquiries, closing old accounts, credit-mix change after paying off a loan, authorized-user exposure, score-version mismatch, report errors). Evergreen, broad household relevance (anyone with a card or planning a mortgage), beginner-to-intermediate depth. The distinctive audience question is 'I did everything right, why did my number fall?' and the practical answer (pay before statement close, keep old cards, check the lender's FICO version, pull all three reports) is concrete and correct in direction. It departs from the channel's dominant mindset and wealth-psychology content toward consumer-credit service content.","Original opportunity: keep the running case-study device (one person, one mortgage meeting, one dollar payoff) but make the arithmetic exact and the case consistent, and anchor each mechanic to the issuer's or FICO's own documentation (statement-date reporting, the 45-day rate-shopping window the script omits, FTC's 5% material-error finding rather than the 40-million extrapolation). A stronger packaging angle may be the dollar consequence ('A 29-point drop cost him $36,000') rather than the mechanism question. Avoid fixed point-loss numbers FICO does not publish.","Same-channel credit/debt service titles sit low: 4eGrsL5CwBQ 832 credit score 0.54383x TYPICAL, J_sTOWazmho car payment hidden math 0.50669x TYPICAL, r4fpD0dgQ64 pay off 10K debt 0.2221x WEAK, gwm1Hr5iipU 50-year mortgage trap 0.32481x WEAK. Aspiration or trap framings do better: mWhpJZrTyNU 2.07599x STRONG, ZnI6pKMnpf4 1.68072x TYPICAL, HEtVmp38D4M 3.64145x STRONG, tynTfEi4518 24.51666x STRONG. External credit-education competitors (bureaus, card-review sites, large finance creators) were not sampled in this review.",,,,
