th investing), while this abstract market-news title performed like other same-channel market-risk titles (0.5x to 1.3x). Dated events described in the script did occur before publication per secondary sources (April CPI 3.8% released May 12; FOMC 8-4 vote April 29; Powell chair term ending May 15; Berkshire record cash reported early May; a 30-year yield above 5.19% around May 19 from low-quality sources only), so the video was topical; a dated event is not proof it drove views and no news catalyst attribution is made. Hypotheses: (a) the vague 'WTF ... Stock Market' title and 'STOCKS DEAD?!' crash image compete with abundant market-news content and may promise a crash the script does not deliver; (b) the 'seven stocks you own' thesis, the script's most original idea, is invisible in packaging; (c) a news-dense script has a short shelf life, limiting long-tail views. Proposed experiment: in owned uploads, test the same script under a concentration title ('You Own 7 Stocks And Don't Know It') with a 401k-holdings thumbnail versus a crash-alarm package, measuring CTR, impressions and 30-second retention. None of these hypotheses is measurable here without impressions, CTR, traffic sources or retention."", ""causal_status"": ""DESCRIPTIVE_ASSOCIATION_NOT_CAUSAL"", ""channel_context"": ""Within-channel comparison holds subscriber base roughly constant; market-risk titles on this channel have clustered in TYPICAL; ten-peer and five-peer tiers disagree."", ""competition"": ""Ten age peers: 4U8h2uiixL4 11.49774x STRONG; HO4L5NJrUz0 0.54653x TYPICAL; ib9B7I8YsRo 0.72474x TYPICAL; vT7IF16WTNg 3.80373x STRONG; TdNH3QP3qao 7.42186x STRONG; Sb0HUHNxF2I 1.87646x TYPICAL; 3iRHI6Fm2cg 0.72846x TYPICAL; yKaD-ExI7tM 0.87766x TYPICAL; dF-_DaVgir0 0.84888x TYPICAL; 7ChF4Frzc_I 0.63218x TYPICAL. Three of ten peers are STRONG, all concrete personal-finance objects; by ten-peer ratio this video ranks fifth of eleven (itself plus ten peers), behind four peers above 1.2x."", ""format_fit"": ""21:37 long-form talking-head-style essay with stacked statistics and a cartoon shock thumbnail; runtime is not watch time."", ""observed_result"": ""8,054 views; 306 likes; 48 comments; 1,297 seconds; 1.20385x TYPICAL ten-peer / 0.29776x WEAK five-peer (peer-sensitive). Public metrics only."", ""original_content_lesson"": {""confidence"": ""HIGH for stored-text claim conflicts (title/thumbnail versus 'near all-time high', MIT metric overstatement, '1992' overstatement); MEDIUM for event dates relayed by secondary sources; LOW for causal virality attribution."", ""test"": ""Produce a concentration-risk video built on dated, sourced index weights and a worked loss example; test concentration-thesis packaging against crash-alarm packaging in owned experiments, measuring CTR, retention at the macro section and drop-off before the action advice.""}, ""review_scope"": ""INDIVIDUAL_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE"", ""source_refs"": [""VIDEO_MASTER.csv:QlPqXGV491Q"", ""TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:QlPqXGV491Q"", ""audit-batches/NICK_148_READ_RECEIPTS.json"", ""PERFORMANCE_SENSITIVITY.csv:QlPqXGV491Q""], ""topic_demand"": ""News-driven market-risk interest; historical search demand and Google Trends unavailable."", ""trend_timing"": ""Published 2026-05-21, nine days after the April CPI release and two days after reported 30-year yield highs, during the Fed chair transition; events verified only via secondary coverage; no causal link to views claimed.""}","{""confidence"": ""UNKNOWN"", ""linkage"": ""No event source_ids attached. Text-only linkage: secondary coverage indicates the April 2026 CPI (3.8%, released May 12), the April 29 FOMC 8-4 statement vote, Powell's chair term ending May 15 and Berkshire's record Q1 cash all preceded the 2026-05-21 publication; the 5.19% 30-year yield is supported only by low-quality mirror pages. Dated events are not proof they drove views."", ""source_ids"": [], ""status"": ""NOT_RESEARCHED"", ""trends_status"": ""UNAVAILABLE""}","{""CTR"": ""UNAVAILABLE_