rtunity: lead with the crossover formula as a personal calculator (your contribution divided by your return) rather than the generic $100K milestone, show the real (inflation-adjusted) version of the ladder, and correct the title promise (at $100K the market still earns less than the saver contributes at typical rates). The Marcus/Dana pairing is reusable story structure."", ""review_scope"": ""FULL_TRANSCRIPT_TOPIC"", ""source_refs"": [""VIDEO_MASTER.csv:QtXhRiEJ9zo"", ""TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:QtXhRiEJ9zo"", ""audit-batches/NICK_150_READ_RECEIPTS.json""]}","{""Age_days"": ""93.0878"", ""Format"": ""LONG_FORM"", ""Lifetime_rate_ratio"": ""0.81903"", ""Metric_snapshot_date"": ""2026-09-11"", ""Peer_Video_IDs"": ""Dgp4_ehMo9k|PWUPOYdwBc8|UmKdQCMCc98|Xtri19wLdJw|poD3PDHgAiE|hDoFNuIDTiI|epARf5FqE_I|ko97I4JNci4|1Ygx1AP3hDA|eU2JB3BP4x0"", ""Peer_count"": ""10"", ""Performance_tier"": ""TYPICAL"", ""Tier_basis"": ""DESCRIPTIVE_LIFETIME_RATE"", ""evidence_kind"": ""OBSERVED_FACT"", ""methodology"": ""METHODS.md; build_baseline.compare""}","{""alternative_explanations"": [""Saturation hypothesis: repeated $100K/compounding uploads may have reduced novelty; traffic data unavailable."", ""Packaging hypothesis: generic premise title without a surprising number; CTR and impressions unavailable."", ""Satisfaction hypothesis: a 4.1% like rate suggests clicked viewers were not dissatisfied; retention unavailable."", ""Confounders: competing STRONG uploads in the same week (bonds, 2026 plan), algorithmic exploration timing, unknown later title or thumbnail edits.""], ""analysis"": ""Observed result: 7,837 frozen views at 93.0878 days; ten-peer ratio 0.81903x TYPICAL and five-peer ratio 0.98956x TYPICAL, both reproduced; tiers agree, so the classification is not peer-sensitive. Likes 320 (4.08% of views) and comments 39 (0.50%). Evidence-backed interpretation: among the ten age peers, the three STRONG videos are a bonds explainer (13.70542x), a 'If I started investing in 2026' plan (3.95720x) and a SpaceX news-adjacent title (6.73434x), while generic money-milestone titles cluster TYPICAL; the same-channel $100K/compounding family splits between STRONG titles with a named rule, ratio or human story and TYPICAL/WEAK plain restatements, and this title belongs to the latter. Hypotheses: (a) the premise had been published repeatedly on this channel, lowering novelty for returning viewers; (b) the title restates a familiar idea without a counterintuitive number, while the thumbnail adds only 'THE $100K RULE'; (c) the letterboxed hqdefault-sized frame wastes about a quarter of its height (cannot tell whether the live thumbnail differs); (d) the relatively high like rate suggests clicked viewers were satisfied, a possible packaging-not-content gap. Proposed experiment: in owned uploads, test the same script under a specific-number title (for example 'Your Last $100K Takes 15 Months. Your First Takes 6.6 Years') versus the generic milestone title, measuring CTR, impressions and 30-second retention. None of these hypotheses is measurable here without impressions, CTR, traffic sources or retention."", ""causal_status"": ""DESCRIPTIVE_ASSOCIATION_NOT_CAUSAL"", ""channel_context"": ""TYPICAL in both peer windows; the channel has published many earlier videos on the same $100K premise, ranging from 0.37449x WEAK to 4.39531x STRONG, so channel size is roughly held constant and the spread is within-channel."", ""competition"": ""Ten age peers: Dgp4_ehMo9k 13.70542x STRONG; PWUPOYdwBc8 3.95720x STRONG; UmKdQCMCc98 0.70008x TYPICAL; Xtri19wLdJw 0.76567x TYPICAL; poD3PDHgAiE 0.44562x WEAK; hDoFNuIDTiI 0.53610x TYPICAL; epARf5FqE_I 1.26861x TYPICAL; ko97I4JNci4 6.73434x STRONG; 1Ygx1AP3hDA 1.30898x TYPICAL; eU2JB3BP4x0 0.25786x WEAK. Three STRONG, five TYPICAL, two WEAK; this video sits in the middle of the TYPICAL band."", ""format_fit"": ""19:20 long-form math explainer with case-study characters, a timeline ladder, caveats and two self-promotion breaks; carto