a the arrow, then the face. At 320px all three text lines remain legible with strong black-on-white contrast; the bill's '$' symbol and the piggy bank are still identifiable, and the face reads as calm and content rather than surprised. The image states a start-to-end transformation ('FROM $100 TO FREEDOM') that is more definite than the title's hedged 'Could Change Your Future', but 'FREEDOM' is abstract and no destination number (such as the script's $350,000) appears. The piggy bank visually signals saving in cash rather than investing, which slightly mismatches the script's central argument that the gain comes from stock-market compounding. The cartoon style matches the generic cartoon-man look seen in other registered Nick Invests thumbnails; whether it is a specific recurring character was not verified. A/B testing, later edits and CTR contribution are unverified.", "coverage": {"Association_verified": "NO", "Historical_design": "UNKNOWN", "Local_asset": "", "Mobile_review": "NOT_REVIEWED", "Thumbnail_URL": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Q2AieN0QhlA/maxresdefault.jpg", "URL_status": "PRESENT_NOT_FETCHED", "Video_ID": "Q2AieN0QhlA"}, "dimensions": [1280, 720], "historical_design": "UNKNOWN", "image_path": "research/finance-economics-intelligence/audit-batches/NICK_Q2AieN0QhlA.jpg", "image_sha256": "876616c62ab6b8a72fa6a35d24bfc9f8212a571aae434c8f2a1f011b86896d78", "image_source": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Q2AieN0QhlA/maxresdefault.jpg", "mobile_review_width": 320, "performance_effect": "NOT_ESTABLISHED", "review_scope": "ACTUAL_IMAGE", "source_refs": ["VIDEO_MASTER.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "THUMBNAIL_COVERAGE.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "audit-batches/NICK_147_READ_RECEIPTS.json"]}, "title": {"analysis": "'How $100 a Month Could Change Your Future' is a concrete-amount, open-outcome title: a small, relatable dollar figure ($100), a recurring cadence (a Month), and a soft, hedged payoff ('Could Change Your Future'). The amount is concrete but the outcome is vague: no end number, no time horizon, no 'math' or 'millionaire' cue, and the modal 'Could' lowers the stakes. Same-channel recurring-contribution and compounding titles split on exactly this dimension. The closest topic twin, vT7IF16WTNg 'Why Everything Changes Once You Invest $100 Per Month', is 3.80373x STRONG; it keeps the $100 figure but adds the channel's 'Why Everything Changes' threshold frame and the verb 'Invest', which tells the viewer the mechanism. Fzdn89C2YXo 'How $500 a Month Makes You a Millionaire (The Surprising Math)' is 3.67806x STRONG with the same 'How $X a Month' opening but a definite verb ('Makes') and a concrete end state ('Millionaire') plus a math parenthetical; hvcr7gVbcr0 '$100,000 Means You're 1/3 Of The Way To $1,000,000 (The Surprising Math)', a contemporaneous age peer, is 2.85698x STRONG; nWkjUETbkkk 'Your Life at Every Level of Compound Interest' 2.03193x STRONG and EjzQXyyREgE 'This is Why Compounding Feels Slow (Until the 7-5-3-1 Rule Kicks In)' 3.43406x STRONG use level/rule structures. Counterexamples that, like this title, promise generic small-amount benefits without a destination number land TYPICAL: 4D90YRoT2yo 'Small Monthly Wins That Can Build $100K' 0.69287x, si24Q4xpT_Y 'Why Small Money Wins Lead to Big Wealth' 0.79722x, tzsM2f6dsEE 'Atomic Money Habits: Small Changes, Compound Results' 0.6133x. Within these eight titles, a definite outcome or explicit math/threshold device co-occurs with STRONG and hedged or generic outcomes with TYPICAL; this is a descriptive pattern, not a cause. Caveat on the twin: vT7IF16WTNg was published 2026-05-19, nine months later, has fewer absolute views (27,553 at about 114 days versus 39,434 at about 398 days), and is ratioed against a different, lower-view peer window, so the 3.80x versus 0.62x gap is relative to channel state at each date, not a clean title A/B.", "peer_comparison_ids": ["vT7IF16WTNg", "Fzdn89C2YXo", "nWkjUETbkkk", "EjzQXyyREgE", "4D90YRoT2yo", "si24Q4xpT_Y", "tzsM2f6dsEE", "hvcr7gVbcr0"], "review_scope": "ACTUAL_TITLE", "script_alignment": "Aligned on the core promise: the script does show what $100 a month could become ($18,000 after 10 years, over $350,000 after 40 years at 8%, 'well over half a million' at 10%). But roughly a quarter of the text is generic habit, discipline and 'opportunity' material that would fit any savings video, and the numeric payoff is concentrated in about 3,600 characters (7,629 to 11,252). 'Change Your Future' is paid off mostly as mindset rather than a concrete plan (no account type, fund, fee or tax discussion).", "search_demand": "Moderate explicit intent: '$100 a month investing' and 'how much will $100 a month grow' are plausible search queries, but the title does not contain 'invest' or a result number. Historical query volume and traffic sources unavailable.", "source_refs": ["VIDEO_MASTER.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "audit-batches/NICK_147_READ_RECEIPTS.json"]}, "topic": {"analysis": "Beginner investing: small recurring contributions plus long-horizon compounding, with a habit/discipline layer. Evergreen; very broad household relevance (the entry amount is deliberately low). Mechanisms: dollar-cost contributions, compound growth, return-on-balance scaling, start-age effect, contribution escalation, pay-yourself-first automation. Distinctive audience question: 'Is $100 a month even worth investing?' The video answers yes with correct nominal arithmetic but omits inflation, fees, taxes and account choice, so the answer is motivational rather than actionable.", "competition": "Same-channel contribution/compounding siblings: vT7IF16WTNg 'Why Everything Changes Once You Invest $100 Per Month' 3.80373x STRONG; Fzdn89C2YXo '$500 a Month Makes You a Millionaire (The Surprising Math)' 3.67806x STRONG; EjzQXyyREgE 7-5-3-1 rule 3.43406x STRONG; nWkjUETbkkk every level of compound interest 2.03193x STRONG; hvcr7gVbcr0 '$100,000 Means You're 1/3 Of The Way' 2.85698x STRONG; generic small-wins siblings 4D90YRoT2yo 0.69287x, si24Q4xpT_Y 0.79722x, tzsM2f6dsEE 0.6133x, all TYPICAL. External competitor coverage not sampled in this review.", "novelty_and_corpus_angle": "Original opportunity: keep the $100 entry point but show the full honest table (7%, 8%, 10% nominal; the same in today's dollars; effect of a 0.5% fee; start at 25 versus 35) and a concrete first-step path (where to put $100, automatic transfer). Use a definite destination in packaging (for example the inflation-adjusted figure as a surprise reversal, or the 40-year nominal figure) rather than 'Could Change Your Future'. Avoid the unsourced 'ahead of 60%' and the millionaire teacher story, which the math contradicts.", "review_scope": "FULL_TRANSCRIPT_TOPIC", "source_refs": ["VIDEO_MASTER.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "audit-batches/NICK_147_READ_RECEIPTS.json"]}, "virality": {"alternative_explanations": ["Packaging hypothesis: hedged outcome ('Could Change Your Future') without a destination number may lower click intent relative to threshold titles; CTR/impressions unavailable.", "Peer-window artefact: the TYPICAL/WEAK split is driven by which neighbours are included; the five-peer window is dominated by unusually STRONG neighbours.", "Content hypothesis: generic, repetitive second half may weaken satisfaction signals; retention unavailable.", "Confounders: algorithmic exploration timing, competition from the channel's own STRONG uploads within days, channel growth between August 2025 and May 2026 when the twin was published, unknown later title/thumbnail edits."], "analysis": "Observed result: 39,434 frozen views at 398.3483 days; ten-peer ratio 0.62280x TYPICAL and five-peer ratio 0.25653x WEAK, both independently reproduced. The tier is peer-sensitive: the ten-peer window includes three WEAK peers that pull the median down, while the five-peer window is dominated by STRONG uploads (Att5nm-UN8M 3.86x, QogQUuyFUx8 4.94x, hvcr7gVbcr0 2.86x), so the classification flips from TYPICAL to WEAK depending on window, and should be reported as TYPICAL-to-WEAK rather than a single tier. Likes 914 (2.32% of views) and comments 70 (0.18%). Evidence-backed interpretation: in its own publication window the channel's STRONG uploads all carried a definite dollar threshold or end state ($100,000 saved fast, live off $500,000, 1/3 of the way to $1,000,000, invest or pay off debt) while this title's outcome is hedged ('Could Change Your Future'); the same split appears in the eight same-channel comparison titles. The later twin vT7IF16WTNg (3.80373x STRONG) shows the $100-per-month topic itself is not a ceiling, but its higher ratio is relative to a different, lower-view peer window nine months later, and it has fewer absolute views, so it is not a controlled comparison. Hypotheses: (a) a hedged outcome with no destination number gives less click intent than the channel's threshold titles; (b) the thumbnail's piggy bank and 'FREEDOM' are abstract and signal saving rather than investing; (c) the long generic motivational tail may have depressed satisfaction signals (like rate 2.32% is lower than some reviewed siblings), though retention is unavailable; (d) the early subscribe request before any value may matter for early drop-off, untestable here. Proposed experiment: in owned uploads, test the same compounding script under a definite-outcome title ('$100 a Month for 40 Years = $349,000 (Or $107,000 After Inflation)') versus a hedged 'could change your future' title, with a matched investing-signalling thumbnail, measuring CTR, impressions and retention at the projection section. None of these hypotheses is measurable here without impressions, CTR, traffic sources or retention.", "causal_status": "DESCRIPTIVE_ASSOCIATION_NOT_CAUSAL", "channel_context": "TYPICAL in the ten-peer window and WEAK in the five-peer window during a stretch where five of ten nearby channel uploads were STRONG; the comparison is within-channel, so channel size is roughly held constant within the window but not across the nine-month gap to vT7IF16WTNg.", "competition": "jZBATMmSBAg 0.63933x TYPICAL; Att5nm-UN8M 3.85935x STRONG; BSlwkVIozNo 0.56009x TYPICAL; QogQUuyFUx8 4.93852x STRONG; hvcr7gVbcr0 2.85698x STRONG; HEtVmp38D4M 3.64145x STRONG; kVpJ1Elw680 0.15245x WEAK; TFtBWn9CWOU 2.11005x STRONG; Ke8nD2zCzmE 0.24125x WEAK; zppYzhlGiOc 0.46591x WEAK. Five of ten age peers are STRONG, all with a definite dollar threshold or decision frame; three are WEAK.", "format_fit": "21:41 long-form motivational explainer with one numeric core section and a long habit/mindset tail; cartoon thumbnail; runtime is not watch time.", "observed_result": "39,434 views; 914 likes; 70 comments; 1,301 seconds; 0.62280x TYPICAL ten-peer / 0.25653x WEAK five-peer (peer-sensitive tier). Public metrics only.", "original_content_lesson": {"confidence": "HIGH for reproduced compounding arithmetic and the 'over $350,000' convention dependence; MEDIUM for the emergency-savings overstatement (secondary and press-release level sources); MEDIUM for the threshold-versus-hedged descriptive pattern; LOW for causal virality attribution.", "test": "Produce a $100-per-month compounding video that discloses the return assumption before the numbers, shows nominal versus inflation-adjusted and fee-adjusted outcomes, and gives one concrete first step; test definite-number packaging against hedged-outcome packaging in owned experiments and measure CTR and retention through the projection section."}, "review_scope": "INDIVIDUAL_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE", "source_refs": ["VIDEO_MASTER.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA", "audit-batches/NICK_147_READ_RECEIPTS.json", "PERFORMANCE_SENSITIVITY.csv:Q2AieN0QhlA"], "topic_demand": "Evergreen beginner-investing topic with plausible search demand for '$100 a month investing'; historical search demand unavailable.", "trend_timing": "Published 2025-08-08; no news catalyst identified or claimed; Google Trends history not fetched."}}
 {"Channel_ID": "UCXzNNA2ngRpRiWvyA7eGd6w", "Video_ID": "QlPqXGV491Q", "batch_id": "NICK_148", "event": {"confidence": "UNKNOWN", "linkage": "No event source_ids attached. Text-only linkage: secondary coverage indicates the April 2026 CPI (3.8%, released May 12), the April 29 FOMC 8-4 statement vote, Powell's chair term ending May 15 and Berkshire's record Q1 cash all preceded the 2026-05-21 publication; the 5.19% 30-year yield is supported only by low-quality mirror pages. Dated events are not proof they drove views.", "source_ids": [], "status": "NOT_RESEARCHED", "trends_status": "UNAVAILABLE"}, "identity": {"Age_days": "112.0965", "Audience_problem": "REQUIRES_SEMANTIC_REVIEW", "Channel": "Nick Invests", "Channel_ID": "UCXzNNA2ngRpRiWvyA7eGd6w", "Classification_method": "TITLE_KEYWORD_HEURISTIC_NOT_SEMANTIC_REVIEW", "Current_views": "NOT_FETCHED", "Dataset": "DS-000022", "Demand_type": "UNVERIFIED", "Duration_seconds": "1297", "Economic_mechanism": "REQUIRES_SEMANTIC_REVIEW", "Evidence_locator": "data/extracted/channel-data/DS-000022/packages/nick-invests/NickInvests_Master_Data.xlsx", "Format": "LONG_FORM", "Format_source_value": "video", "Lifetime_rate_ratio": "1.20385", "Metadata_source": "data/catalog/youtube_channel_registry.db:videos:QlPqXGV491Q", "Metric_snapshot_date": "2026-09-11", "Narrative_angle": "UNVERIFIED", "Peer_Video_IDs": "4U8h2uiixL4|HO4L5NJrUz0|ib9B7I8YsRo|vT7IF16WTNg|TdNH3QP3qao|Sb0HUHNxF2I|3iRHI6Fm2cg|yKaD-ExI7tM|dF-_DaVgir0|7ChF4Frzc_I", "Peer_count": "10", "Performance_tier": "TYPICAL", "Published_at_raw": "2026-05-21 21:41:01", "Snapshot_precision": "SOURCE_DECLARED_SCRAPE_DAY_TIMEZONE_UNKNOWN", "Tier_basis": "DESCRIPTIVE_LIFETIME_RATE", "Time_sensitivity": "UNVERIFIED", "Title": "WTF Is Happening To The Stock Market?!", "Topic_tags_provisional": "investing", "URL": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QlPqXGV491Q", "Video_ID": "QlPqXGV491Q", "Views": "8054", "comments": 48, "description": "Thanks for watching\n\nDisclaimer: The purpose is t