LIST' is small enough that the typo is hard to notice. Relation to title and script: 'WIN BY AVOIDING LOSS' restates the inversion premise in plainer words than the title and is a better summary of the script's actual thesis (avoid mistakes) than 'Do the Opposite'. 'Impulsive shopping' and 'high-interest credit card' correspond to script items (emotional spending, credit cards); 'broken contract' does not correspond to any of the 11 items in the stored text. The blank checklist promises a list, which the script delivers (11 items), though the title does not. No Munger, Buffett or inversion visual appears. Historical continuity, A/B testing and CTR contribution are unverified.", "coverage": {"Association_verified": "NO", "Historical_design": "UNKNOWN", "Local_asset": "", "Mobile_review": "NOT_REVIEWED", "Thumbnail_URL": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/QtlJUTJ58ZU/maxresdefault.jpg", "URL_status": "PRESENT_NOT_FETCHED", "Video_ID": "QtlJUTJ58ZU"}, "dimensions": [1280, 720], "historical_design": "UNKNOWN", "image_path": "research/finance-economics-intelligence/audit-batches/NICK_QtlJUTJ58ZU.jpg", "image_sha256": "5789e078928edc0afefcba185ce52a1e2b224cf1f91d62d88b281c2f83f71416", "image_source": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/QtlJUTJ58ZU/maxresdefault.jpg", "mobile_review_width": 320, "performance_effect": "NOT_ESTABLISHED", "review_scope": "ACTUAL_IMAGE", "source_refs": ["VIDEO_MASTER.csv:QtlJUTJ58ZU", "THUMBNAIL_COVERAGE.csv:QtlJUTJ58ZU", "audit-batches/NICK_151_READ_RECEIPTS.json"]}, "title": {"analysis": "'Do the Opposite: The Wealth Trick Rich People Use (Inversion Thinking)' is a three-part title: an imperative paradox ('Do the Opposite'), a secret-of-the-rich promise ('The Wealth Trick Rich People Use') and a named mental model in parentheses ('Inversion Thinking'). It contains no number, dollar figure, object or time marker, and 'the opposite' of what is never stated, so the curiosity gap is wide but vague. It belongs to the channel's 'named rule or mental model' family, which