s a group use this method. The title implies one trick; the video delivers an unannounced list of 11.", "search_demand": "Some explicit search intent for 'inversion thinking' as a mental-model term, but it is a niche query; 'wealth trick rich people use' is a browse/suggested phrasing. Historical query volume and traffic sources unavailable.", "source_refs": ["VIDEO_MASTER.csv:QtlJUTJ58ZU", "TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:QtlJUTJ58ZU", "audit-batches/NICK_151_READ_RECEIPTS.json"]}, "topic": {"analysis": "Personal-finance mental model (Munger-style inversion) applied as a list of 11 wealth-destroying habits: believing income is the problem, credit cards, lifestyle inflation, status spending, no emergency fund, financial illiteracy, procrastination, complexity, emotional decisions, social environment, home equity extraction. Evergreen; beginner audience; broad household relevance. Distinctive audience question: 'Is there a simpler way to get ahead than trying harder?' The answer is avoidance-based, but most items overlap with the channel's existing 'wealth killers' and 'mistakes to avoid' videos, so the inversion label is the main novelty.", "competition": "Same-channel named-rule siblings are mostly TYPICAL: EwbXdhQ0qrw 80/20 Rule 0.90095x, MV3oBl8OPfM Eat the Frog 1.0592x; v-1VwbsUa94 Chinese Rule 2.57622x STRONG. Avoidance/mistakes siblings: e06r3ZWyBVc 0.82458x TYPICAL, NAg-Xx_xy8U 0.4978x WEAK, JtMc-fNjfpo 0.49581x WEAK. Concrete 'how the rich actually' mechanism 7W0uvrGuOW4 5.76468x STRONG. External competitor coverage of Munger inversion not sampled in this review.", "novelty_and_corpus_angle": "Original opportunity: actually perform an inversion on screen, writing the 'how to stay poor' list and converting each item to a specific opposite rule with a number (for example 20%-plus card APR versus paying in full, the rate-dependent early-investor example with its 6.1% break-even shown honestly, the 30-year value of a $500 payment at 7%), and attribute Jacobi and Munger 