rer than the title but its small folder labels are unreadable on mobile; (c) the video was surrounded by several same-week mindset uploads (80/20 Rule, Atomic Money Habits, Not-So-Smart People) competing for the same audience; (d) the long setup before the first list item may limit retention. Proposed experiment: in owned uploads, test a concrete inversion title (for example '11 Ways to Guarantee You Stay Broke (Do the Opposite)') against the abstract 'Do the Opposite' title, and test a version that reaches item 1 within the first 90 seconds; measure CTR, impressions and retention at the first list item. None of these hypotheses is measurable here without impressions, CTR, traffic sources or retention.", "causal_status": "DESCRIPTIVE_ASSOCIATION_NOT_CAUSAL", "channel_context": "TYPICAL in both peer windows in a week where nine of ten peers were also TYPICAL; the within-channel comparison holds channel size roughly constant, so the gap to 'Buy, Borrow, Die' is not explained by audience size.", "competition": "7W0uvrGuOW4 5.76468x STRONG; EwbXdhQ0qrw 0.90095x TYPICAL; MKSPz6cWlwc 0.62535x TYPICAL; tzsM2f6dsEE 0.6133x TYPICAL; DbLgEsEUojA 1.58543x TYPICAL; bYmB2S2h_B4 1.73944x TYPICAL; UdfpP8R1zuI 0.89446x TYPICAL; D-8FxjgbCeY 0.59518x TYPICAL; -j4OlDr1rcc 1.2279x TYPICAL; VREo0Hj_tyQ 1.14397x TYPICAL. One of ten age peers is STRONG and none WEAK; this video sits in the lower TYPICAL cluster with other abstract mindset titles.", "format_fit": "21:51 long-form mindset essay: about a third setup, then an unannounced 11-item list; cartoon thumbnail; runtime is not watch time.", "observed_result": "19,992 views; 616 likes; 66 comments; 1,311 seconds; 0.69140x TYPICAL ten-peer / 0.72501x TYPICAL five-peer. Public metrics only.", "original_content_lesson": {"confidence": "HIGH for stored-text claim issues (lottery overstatement, loss-aversion mislabel, unstated rate assumptions) and compounding arithmetic; MEDIUM for Jacobi attribution (no primary source located) and the concrete-versus-abstract descriptive pattern; LOW for causal virality attribution.", "test": "Produce an inversion video that announces the item count up front, reaches item 1 within 90 seconds, pairs each 'how to stay poor' item with an explicit opposite rule and one verified number, and attributes Jacobi/Munger accurately; test concrete-list packaging against abstract 'do the opposite' packaging in owned experiments, measuring CTR and retention at the first list item."}, "review_scope": "INDIVIDUAL_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE", "source_refs": ["VIDEO_MASTER.csv:QtlJUTJ58ZU", "TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:QtlJUTJ58ZU", "audit-batches/NICK_151_READ_RECEIPTS.json", "PERFORMANCE_SENSITIVITY.csv:QtlJUTJ58ZU"], "topic_demand": "Evergreen money-mindset and mental-model content; 'inversion thinking' has niche search interest; historical search demand unavailable.", "trend_timing": "Published 2025-12-12 during a dense daily-upload run; no news catalyst identified or claimed (Munger died 2023-11-28, more than a year earlier, and is not referenced as news); Google Trends history not fetched."}}
