 was not matched to a named source; treat as PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED. Primary Stanger data not opened.", "'You get 5% a quarter, so it takes you 5 years to leave': 20 quarters x 5% = 100% only if each quarter you receive 5% of your original holding. If the fund repurchases 5% of shares outstanding and every holder requests 100%, each holder receives 5% of the remaining balance each quarter, so after 20 quarters about 35.8% is still unredeemed (0.95^20 = 0.358, analyst calculation) and full exit never mathematically completes. If only a minority request, exit is faster. The narrator correctly says this is 'the flattering version', but the 5-year figure is a simplification, not a ceiling.", "'Alvin asked for 80,000 and got half': $40,000 / $80,000 = 50% (analyst calculation), consistent with the stated 53% average fulfilment. Alvin, Karina and Erica are presented as real people with no sourcing; UNVERIFIED and likely composite or illustrative.", "'Last November, Blue Owl proposed merging two of its own funds ... roughly 80 cents on the dollar ... The deal collapsed in 48 hours': the OBDC/OBDC II merger was terminated effective 18 November 2025 and announced 19 November 2025 (SEC 8-K exhibit; trade coverage), citing market conditions, with reports that OBDC II holders faced a redemption pause and potential losses from OBDC trading below NAV. The 'roughly 80 cents' exchange-ratio estimate and the '48 hours' timing were not confirmed in this review; the merger had been announced earlier in November per secondary coverage. Later '$1.4 billion of assets ... wind the fund down' UNVERIFIED.", "'One Prospect Capital disclosed a discount near 57%. ... offering you 43 cents': arithmetic consistent (1 - 0.57 = 0.43). The discount figure and the group-wide '25% below stated book value' were not checked; UNVERIFIED.", "'Last August, an executive order told the Labor Department ... and this March, it proposed the rule handing your employer a safe harbor': confirmed. Executive Order 143