f these hypotheses is measurable here without impressions, CTR, traffic sources or retention.","5,344 views; 276 likes; 45 comments; 1,212 seconds; 0.49765x WEAK ten-peer / 0.47287x WEAK five-peer. Public metrics only.",Evergreen consumer-credit question with plausible steady search demand; historical search volume unavailable.,Published 2026-04-08 in a dense daily-upload window; no dated news catalyst is tied to the video (the CFPB actions it cites were from January 2025); Google Trends history not fetched.,"mErWx9GiVUc 0.77667x TYPICAL; eAzo0uvSnus 0.72657x TYPICAL; zwrY8QsDTgs 1.86362x TYPICAL; 4eGrsL5CwBQ 0.54383x TYPICAL; ypUI1Sv-Nhk 2.18459x STRONG; R_E6OOnF9e4 0.59678x TYPICAL; 8rhg_K7c4O8 4.84661x STRONG; f6HIYQUiMoU 33.03103x STRONG; ccNuYRhrA0U 1.00027x TYPICAL; 8LncpNMNPW8 0.31287x WEAK. Three of ten age peers are STRONG, six TYPICAL, and this video is one of two WEAK in the window alongside 8LncpNMNPW8.","20:12 long-form explainer with a running case study, labelled trap sections and a five-step action close; cartoon thumbnail; runtime is not watch time.","WEAK in both peer windows in a week where a news reaction and broad wealth lists were STRONG; comparison is within-channel so subscriber base is roughly constant, but topic audience differs between credit service content and wealth-identity content.","[""Audience-fit hypothesis: credit-score repair content may draw a different, smaller audience than the channel's wealth-mindset core; traffic and audience data unavailable."", ""Cannibalization hypothesis: 4eGrsL5CwBQ, another credit-score title three days earlier, may have absorbed demand; impressions unavailable."", ""Packaging hypothesis: no number or dollar stakes in title or thumbnail, and the topic label on the phone is illegible on mobile; CTR unavailable."", ""Confounders: algorithmic exploration timing, the extreme housing-market outlier f6HIYQUiMoU in the same window, unknown later title or thumbnail edits.""]","{""confidence"": ""HIGH for mortgage and utilization arithmetic and for the FTC, myFICO inquiry and CFPB enforcement checks; MEDIUM for the within-channel descriptive pattern; LOW for causal virality attribution."", ""test"": ""Produce a credit-mechanics explainer with one consistent case study whose payoff number is exactly computed (about 36,600 dollars for 0.4 points on 380,000 dollars over 30 years), include the rate-shopping window and FTC's 5% material-error finding, and test a dollar-stakes package against a mechanism-question package in owned experiments; measure CTR, search share, and retention at each case-study callback.""}",DESCRIPTIVE_ASSOCIATION_NOT_CAUSAL,
+R_E6OOnF9e4,UCXzNNA2ngRpRiWvyA7eGd6w,Nick Invests,15 Low Effort Boring Tasks That Make More Than Your Job,6609,TYPICAL,2026-09-11,COMPLETE_LIMITED_EVIDENCE,INDIVIDUAL_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE,"[""VIDEO_MASTER.csv:R_E6OOnF9e4"", ""TRANSCRIPT_COVERAGE.csv:R_E6OOnF9e4"", ""audit-batches/NICK_154_READ_RECEIPTS.json"", ""PERFORMANCE_SENSITIVITY.csv:R_E6OOnF9e4""]","Observed result: 6,609 frozen views at 151.1351 days; ten-peer ratio 0.59678x TYPICAL and five-peer ratio 0.66659x TYPICAL, both independently reproduced; the tier agrees across peer windows but sits in the lower part of the TYPICAL band, about 0.1 above the WEAK boundary. Likes 289 (4.37% of views) and comments 46 (0.70%). Evidence-backed interpretation: among its ten age peers, the two STRONG videos carry concrete self-comparison or object hooks ('15 Signs You Are Actually Doing Better Than the Average Person' 2.18459x, 'Why Everything Changes After Paying Off Your Car Loan' 3.43336x), and the channel's dollar-anchored passive-income titles (HWU9IQB9Q-k 2.27303x, vdMkNfJYqLI 2.00183x, xtdEdCdznsg 2.18248x) outperform this effort-adjective list; this is a descriptive pattern only. Hypotheses: (a) the title's comparative 'more than your job' promise without a dollar figure may read as generic side-hustle content, a crowded genre; (b) the thumbnail's icon grid advertises streams (Affiliate, Ebooks, Airbnb, Car Rental) not in the video, and its 320px labels are hard to read, so packaging may neither stand out nor match; (c) the relatively high like rate may indicate viewers who clicked found the specific, caveated delivery useful, a possible packaging-not-content gap. Proposed experiment: in owned uploads, test the same script under a dollar-anchored title using the honest outcome (for example 'How a $58K Earner Built $1,300 a Month in Side Income') and a thumbnail that shows the script's actual items, versus an effort-adjective title, and measure CTR, impressions, 30-second retention and retention across the item-6 category pivot. None of these hypotheses is measurable here without impressions, CTR, traffic sources or retention.","6,609 views; 289 likes; 46 comments; 1,415 seconds; 0.59678x TYPICAL ten-peer / 0.66659x TYPICAL five-peer. Public metrics only.",Evergreen side-income/passive-income content with persistent search and browse interest; historical search demand unavailable.,Published 2026-04-12 near US tax-filing season in a dense daily-upload window; no news catalyst identified or claimed; Google Trends history not fetched.,"ypUI1Sv-Nhk 2.18459x STRONG; ccNuYRhrA0U 1.00027x TYPICAL; zwrY8QsDTgs 1.86362x TYPICAL; 8LncpNMNPW8 0.31287x WEAK; eAzo0uvSnus 0.72657x TYPICAL; vXBhBlBIUDs 3.43336x STRONG; RUVOjfrIemY 0.49765x WEAK; 1W9dzLgpU4k 0.54346x TYPICAL; mErWx9GiVUc 0.77667x TYPICAL; -DIT32sBkAk 1.98045x TYPICAL. Two STRONG, six TYPICAL, two WEAK; this video ranks eighth of eleven on lifetime-rate ratio.",23:35 long-form numbered listicle (15 items) with a running composite-character story; cartoon thumbnail with icon grid; runtime is not watch time.,"Lower TYPICAL in both peer windows during a week where the channel had two STRONG uploads; the comparison is within-channel, so subscriber base is roughly held constant.","[""Packaging hypothesis: an undollared comparative promise in a saturated side-hustle genre may lower click intent; CTR/impressions unavailable."", ""Packaging-mismatch hypothesis: thumbnail icons promise streams the video does not cover; any effect on satisfaction or retention is unmeasured."", ""Saturation hypothesis: frequent channel uploads that week may have competed for the same audience; traffic data unavailable."", ""Confounders: algorithmic exploration timing, competition from the channel's own STRONG uploads that week, unknown later title/thumbnail edits.""]","{""confidence"": ""HIGH for stored-text internal contradictions (vending, print on demand, Mary ledger capital) and tax-treatment errors; MEDIUM for the dollar-anchored versus effort-adjective descriptive pattern; LOW for causal virality attribution."", ""test"": ""Produce a side-income list where every earnings figure is a typical or median value with a named source, Mary-style composite examples are arithmetically reconciled with the stated salary and timeline, and tax treatment per stream is stated; test dollar-anchored honest packaging against effort-adjective packaging in owned experiments and measure CTR, retention at the category pivot, and comment sentiment about credibility.""}",DESCRIPTIVE_ASSOCIATION_NOT_CAUSAL,
